## Crate Architecture

| Crate | Layer | Responsibility |
|-------|-------|----------------|
| `{{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-domain` | Domain | Entities, value objects, policies, domain services. **Zero external deps.** |
| `{{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-application` | Application | Commands, use-case handlers, port traits, orchestration |
| `{{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-infrastructure` | Infrastructure | SQLite, filesystem, settings, logging. Implements port traits. |
| `{{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-desktop` | Presentation | Tauri host, command bridge, state management, window lifecycle |

## Mandatory Architecture Rules

1. **Dependency direction**: Domain ← Application ← Infrastructure ← Desktop. Never reverse.
2. **Domain purity**: `{{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-domain` has zero dependencies on other crates or external I/O.
3. **Port-adapter pattern**: Application defines port traits. Infrastructure implements them.
4. **Command-oriented flow**: UI actions dispatch application commands. No event-driven foundation.
5. **Local-first persistence**: SQLite via rusqlite. WAL mode. Embedded migrations.
6. **Tauri commands are thin**: Desktop crate dispatches to application layer. No business logic in commands.

